{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1215363-sources-of-inspiration","id":1215363,"title":"Sources of Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-04T22:13:04-07:00","id":1215363,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Sources of Inspiration","content":"So, it saddens me a little bit to make this post. It saddens me because I feel like I've run out of gas on Exalted. In a game full of heroes of myth and legends, with world scarring panoplies, and names that resound throughout a direction, I've run out of inspiration.<br /> <br /> At the beginning of the campaign I'm currently in, I found stunt fodder in just about everything. No scene was too bland while I was in it, because I could always shape it a little more with a well worded stunt or a bit of ardent essence. And my character was always doing something, as is the nature of the Exalted. When she wasn't preparing to raid another Linowan settlement she was perfecting her beast-taming abilities or showing one of her siblings all the terrible things they could do with quick fingers, a cloak, and a fist full of knives as opposed to the standard Haltan boomerang. But as of late, I'm barely stunting anymore, and I've found that I can barely come up with her next Motivation after she and the circle tore through the Linowan lines and secured victory for Halta in the Haltan/Linowan war. What does she do next? Where does her story lead her to next? And it's beginning to effect the other PC's who note her lack of action lately. Yes, she's still doing smaller things. She's still prideful, and will flirt with just about anyone who walks past while keeping a hand on their gold-purse. But she hasn't caused any significant change where she's been. She hasn't even deigned to keep eye on a small tribe as Lunars of her age tend to do.<br /> <br /> It's hurting the game I'm preparing to GM as well. One of the DB's I was especially excited to flesh out just came off as... bland? And after the DBWFHW manuscript previews? He should be more interesting than ever! But for some reason I've been missing the spark in just about all of my Exalted materials. They've started to feel less heroes of legend and more just superpowered adults. So here I am to ask the community for some help finding sources of inspiration for their characters and settings. Yes, there is a list at the front of each book, but I want to hear from the Exalted community itself. Maybe there's a bit of spark in Spongebob Squarepants and his theatrics that you just aren't going to find in The House of Flying Daggers, or a more Lunar tone to Mogley from the Jungle Book than from Sun-Wukong in Journey to the East?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13053-dxzstar","name":"Dxzstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13053_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T03:33:36-07:00","id":1215431,"title":"","content":"The Steve Erikson about the Malazan empire or rather in the empire, is a newfound and great Joy for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T06:24:03-07:00","id":1215462,"title":"","content":"Hmm...Steven Erikson's Malazan: Book of the Fallen has some pretty great inspiration for Exalts with the 'ascendants', with Elders like Anomander Rake all the way to young bullheaded youngsters who are out to prove their might to the world (Karza Oo'lan). <br /> <br /> The Recent God of War game I found is a bit of fantastic inspiration.<br /> <br /> Codex Alera is listed in WFHW's inspriation page and its got a lot of interesting things being done with the elements by the roman styled civilisation that the books foccus on, though the latter two books seem to take that away a bit .<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:50:14-07:00","id":1215492,"title":"","content":"While actually mentioned in the books already, <b>Lord of Light</b> by Roger Zelazny is pretty great and I highly recommend it in general.<br /> <br /> <b>The Years of Rice and Salt</b> by Kim Stanley Robinson was one of my favorite books in the last while. The later chapters get into stuff that isn't so Exalted-reelvant, but the first half or so of the book when we are in the pre-Industrial Era of the setting is pretty awesome to me for being a ficitonal persepctive of the historic world pretty different than what we get a lot in fiction and an altenrative history well out of the Big Cliche Settings (American Revolution Success, Civil War Success, WWII stuff). It is a great source for ideas of stuff to put into your games themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Debt: the First 5,000 Years</b> by David Graeber made being a merchant, banker, member of the Guild, and all that really itneresting. It's also, again, a really good book I think for just giving ideas of what's out in the world to draw on for Creation itself.<br /> <br /> <b>Zealot: the Life and Times of Jesus of Nazareth</b> is an intersting book by Raza Aslan which tries to piece together what the political world around a historical Jesus woul dhave been, looking at sources out of the Bible to talk about htings like the zealots in early Judeah, the early Church's evolution, Roman views on the Jewish provinces, and so on. It's an interesting snapshot of the ancient world to me and I liked it a lot for giving me ideas of what Roman imperialism looked like in practice and how people responded to it in the time.<br /> <br /> <b>The Grace of Kings</b> by Ken Liu is a really neat Chinese-inspired fantasy setting which manages to keep its scale in good check and presents I think a pretty enjoyable story. Kind of hard to say a lot else that doesn't spoil it, but I think it's worth a shot for something pretty different when it comes to politically-driven fantasy compared to what we often get in media.<br /> <br /> <b>Night's Master</b> and the rest of the Flat Earth series by Tanith Lee is probably the most influenential to Exalted books ever, and I think that reading it gave me a completely different eview on how to approach a lot of things in Exalted as a whole. Really worth a read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T10:03:58-07:00","id":1215539,"title":"","content":"First off...if a character has accomplished a ton of stuff and built a legend and you aren't finding her as engaging to play...well, consider playing a different character for a while. I tend to give this advice more often with relationships than games, but... sometimes you just need to try something new.<br /> <br /> In terms of general loss of the spark for the setting, I find the key to finding that engagement again is often to narrow your focus. It's easier to care about a single family or a single village than an empire, and if you're doing a lot of Fate of Nations/Save the World scale plots lately you can start to find it harder to care about the backdrop. Focus on mythology and soap opera inspiration: love, hate, jealousy, webs of lies. When in doubt, fall in love with someone you shouldn't, that always seems to work when I am not sure what to do with a PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T23:09:07-07:00","id":1215996,"title":"","content":"**Spice and Wolf** is great for exploring what kind of trouble Bereaucracy focused Exalt and a local wolf god can get themselves into. I really like how the challenges are essentially white collar crimes of Late Medieval / Renaissance Europe. Craft Lawrence is my go to for how Bereaucracy works and how much fun noncombat plots can be. <br /> <br /> **One Piece** is a great adventure island hopping campaign, with Sail challenges, the jackboot of the Realm, and a ton of combat monsters going at it. It also has TONS of stunt inspiration when the weaker members fight or the power trio take on a stronger foe (Nami's &quot;climatact&quot; is essentially a Black and Blue Jade Weather Control Staff).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}